    "experience_text": "Use the matched guidance together where supported by the current task and source. If advice conflicts, resolve it against the concrete requirements and explain the choice; do not combine incompatible obligations.\n\nMatched experience 092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce\n092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce:R01 [Applicability]\nSaving or subscription cleanup synchronously calls host listeners that may open another document or close the workspace.\n\n092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce:R02 [Event relation]\nCapture the old view and remove its current ownership. Finish final old-view effects, such as clearing its display, before callback-capable saving, or check authority for effects remaining after callbacks. An outer open rechecks its request identity after retirement.\n\n092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce:R03 [Preservation]\nNested open/close, nested editing and the new view's rendering remain authoritative. Disposal also cleans up captured resources rather than clearing objects installed by a callback.\n\n092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce:R04 [Exclusion]\nProtecting only final view installation can still leave a later stale clearing render. Do not require every host to detach first; notification order follows the current contract.\n\n092e85e09f09609c924bb3d41747f72d8a7558392eccffd0341e8694cee4fdce:R05 [Verification]\nInvoke open/close inside listeners for timer-driven and departure-driven saves. Check document output, subscriptions and nested edits after the outer call returns, through both direct calls and actual unmounting.\n\n\nMatched experience 020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892\n020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892:R01 [Applicability]\nStartup, cleanup, saving or publication can synchronously reenter navigation and install a new owner.\n\n020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892:R02 [Event relation]\nCapture old resources and publish retirement before callback-capable work. Establish provisional cleanup ownership before startup where needed. After callbacks, recheck request and owner identity before installing a returned handle or publishing a destination.\n\n020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892:R03 [Preservation]\nComplete cleanup for captured old resources without clearing or taking ownership of a newer visit. Preserve the documented idempotent cleanup behavior.\n\n020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892:R04 [Exclusion]\nDo not assume code after a synchronous callback still owns the current view. Do not hard-code one cleanup ordering when the current API requires a different order; guard remaining effects.\n\n020a49e031c6debee42b6737e3b521faebbb5394e908c26ddf24d6e2fc2d9892:R05 [Verification]\nExercise hide, switch and dispose inside startup, detachment and saving; check both resulting view and resource ownership after the outer call returns.\n\n\nMatched experience bc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e\nbc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e:R01 [Applicability]\nEvents belong to a specific visit or attempt, and startup can deliver more events before its cleanup capability returns.\n\nbc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e:R02 [Event relation]\nCheck the originating owner before admitting each event. Retire logical admission immediately when that owner ends, independently of when physical detachment becomes available.\n\nbc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e:R03 [Preservation]\nPreviously admitted work has separate completion and effect obligations. Reopening the same source creates a new visit when the current contract defines it that way.\n\nbc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e:R04 [Exclusion]\nDo not treat source or file identity as visit identity. Do not infer that retirement cancels already-admitted work.\n\nbc95102b5f0452a13fac0570a43c65bd195826406c0d979c3cea47c74ad6c59e:R05 [Verification]\nDuring multi-event startup, let the first callback hide or replace its owner. Check rejection of later old-owner events and valid reception by the new owner.\n\n\nMatched experience 8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c\n8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c:R01 [Applicability]\nA framework component or workspace wrapper exposes the coordinator. Correct direct calls do not establish correct component unmounting.\n\n8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c:R02 [Event relation]\nFollow the current integration's actual call path for dispose, subscription removal and navigation ownership. Do not import lifecycle behavior from another framework version.\n\n8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c:R03 [Preservation]\nPreserve the interfaces actually present: React effect cleanup, Vue 2 beforeDestroy, Vue 3 onBeforeUnmount/expose, jQuery events or the corresponding native entry points.\n\n8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c:R04 [Exclusion]\nThese are alternatives from different cases, not requirements for one project to implement together. A native embedding does not imply a DOM or Promise runtime.\n\n8aacd6e164e2a8fc5c967472fac5b0b34b0b06a9879a206a213ab1f138e1460c:R05 [Verification]\nCheck both public coordinator calls and actual component unmounting. Navigate inside an unmount-triggered save and check the new view, externally callable APIs and resource release.\n\n\nMatched experience 9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R01 [Applicability]\nA source may be reused across visits, attempts or selections of the same file object. Each opening has its own UI lifetime.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R02 [Event relation]\nControl effects with actual visit or attempt identity, not equality of files, channels or transport objects. Later visits obtain their own bootstrap and streaming updates.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R03 [Preservation]\nPreserve shared-source reuse, independent workspaces, subsequent valid uses and existing attempt management.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R04 [Exclusion]\nDo not permanently stop a shared source to suppress old results or let reopening the same object revive a retired visit's publication permission.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R05 [Verification]\nReopen the same object and channel, complete old decoding late and interleave two independent workspaces. Check isolation of old effects and continued operation of the new visit.\n",
